 17592186045463 13194139535632 true] [17592186358496 1100 "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨1,\\,t⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\frac{t}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}},\\,\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535632 true] [17592186358496 1113 #uuid "cc02cdb1-2d7d-5481-92b3-bd104f553197" 13194139535632 true] [17592186358496 1145 "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{t}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{2}}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3}}+\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535632 true] [17592186358497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358498 13194139535632 true] [17592186358497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358499 13194139535632 true] [17592186358497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358500 13194139535632 true] [17592186358497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358501 13194139535632 true] [17592186358497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358502 13194139535632 true] [17592186358497 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535632 true] [17592186358497 1041 "selection" 13194139535632 true] [17592186358497 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358502 13194139535632 true] [17592186358497 1110 #uuid "7a285d2b-c3a3-50ff-b767-87c82d5357d6" 131941395356